name: simple-rest
version: '@VERSION@'
summary: REST and TCP client in one file, with its UI in the browser
description: |
  simple-rest is a Postman-like REST client that is a single program. It
  serves its interface on http://127.0.0.1:8787/ and sends the requests
  itself, so CORS never gets in the way: collections, history, environments
  with variables, schedules that keep a token fresh, and a TCP console for
  devices on the network (LF, CR LF, MLLP and STX/ETX framing).

  The snap keeps its data in ~/snap/simple-rest/common. Start it with
  `simple-rest -listen 0.0.0.0:8787` to reach the UI from another machine on
  a network you trust.
license: MIT
base: core24
confinement: strict
grade: stable
architectures: [@ARCH@]
apps:
  simple-rest:
    command: simple-rest
    plugs: [network, network-bind, desktop]
